Cell["\<\
It is a cap by ARRIVAL ORDER, not a uniform draw, and which states arrive \
first depends on the schedule. Two runs of the same input can therefore keep \
different states, and the states kept are not a uniform sample of the ones \
available: capping clips the offspring distribution to a point mass.\
\>", "ExampleText",
 CellID->581644275,ExpressionUUID->"79d0371a-30a6-04e5-2fef-af4441536ecf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Use ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<TransitionRate\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d950d76-dd18-2b24-2baa-a533d4ad760e"],
 " for sampling that is uniform and reproducible. A rate is defined per \
transition and needs no notion of a step, so it needs no barrier, it is drawn \
from the transition's own identity and the seed rather than from arrival \
order, and it preserves the branching structure a sample exists to \
represent."
}], "ExampleText",
 CellID->741181503,ExpressionUUID->"7234a9f4-3232-6781-23cb-40be47c74deb"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Graph options", "ExampleSubsection",
 CellID->147747426,ExpressionUUID->"42668d78-f434-72a4-721d-2525fdc1408e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every option of ",
 Cell[BoxData["Graph"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c7cc198-0ad8-2426-3403-d8c2af528f0c"],
 " is also an option of ",
 Cell[BoxData["HGEvolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "69698b1d-3dc2-3628-1f16-2347b4749d72"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["HGSessionOpen"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "701e1eb7-eeba-61c8-2025-97f08b4f3312"],
 ", and goes to the graph a graph property returns. A value given in the call \
replaces the default, such as the layered layout:"
}], "ExampleText",
 CellID->2026698593,ExpressionUUID->"0e322415-281a-3695-37c1-be5f49ac9cff"],

